WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.601 --> 00:00:14.831
Oh, hello.

2
00:00:15.431 --> 00:00:16.552
Welcome to our home.

3
00:00:17.613 --> 00:00:21.976
I'm Jo March and I'm here to share with you a little about the story you are going

4
00:00:22.017 --> 00:00:22.497
to read.

5
00:00:25.359 --> 00:00:28.182
As you may know, it is entitled Little Women.

6
00:00:29.142 --> 00:00:36.632
It's a story about my family─well, more specifically, about me and my three sisters: Meg, who is the

7
00:00:36.732 --> 00:00:41.957
oldest; Beth, who is a couple of years younger than me; and the baby of the family, Amy.

8
00:00:43.478 --> 00:00:48.962
Our story is based on the true-life story of the author, Louisa May Alcott, who also had three

9
00:00:49.042 --> 00:00:54.607
sisters. Louisa May Alcott was born on November 29, 1832.

10
00:00:57.436 --> 00:01:01.298
Like me, she was the second daughter in a family of four girls.

11
00:01:02.419 --> 00:01:05.800
Louisa grew up in Concord, Massachusetts, USA.

12
00:01:06.721 --> 00:01:09.442
From a young age, Louisa loved to write.

13
00:01:10.323 --> 00:01:13.664
She wrote poetry and even several thrillers, believe it or not.

14
00:01:14.625 --> 00:01:20.508
She was also an avid reader, fueling her imagination with works from Shakespeare to Charlotte Bronte.

15
00:01:22.192 --> 00:01:27.335
As you read Little Women, you may see a strong resemblance between my character and Louisa.

16
00:01:28.416 --> 00:01:36.341
In fact, according to Louisa, she did indeed base my character on herself, while her real sisters─Anna, Lizzie,

17
00:01:36.361 --> 00:01:40.063
and May─ are depicted by Meg, Beth, and Amy respectively.

18
00:01:42.364 --> 00:01:44.125
Little Women was published in 1868.

19
00:01:44.405 --> 00:01:48.228
The story is set during the American Civil War.

20
00:01:49.224 --> 00:01:52.986
Father is away at war, not as a soldier, but as a chaplain.

21
00:01:53.927 --> 00:01:59.731
He is a very thoughtful, kind man, who instills in us, his daughters, a strong sense of morals

22
00:01:59.931 --> 00:02:01.011
and family values.

23
00:02:02.152 --> 00:02:07.976
At one time Father used to be very rich but now, after the war, our family is struggling

24
00:02:08.036 --> 00:02:12.999
financially. Mother is the most loving, caring person in the world.

25
00:02:13.619 --> 00:02:19.856
She is not perfect, but she makes every effort to help us girls learn life's important lessons, as

26
00:02:19.936 --> 00:02:23.039
well as treasure the moments we share together as a family.

27
00:02:25.141 --> 00:02:31.306
My sister Meg is a lovely person who has a strong sense of responsibility and looks after her

28
00:02:31.366 --> 00:02:32.287
younger sisters.

29
00:02:33.868 --> 00:02:37.431
Meg does have her faults, though, and one of them is vanity.

30
00:02:38.392 --> 00:02:42.276
She longs to have fashionable, pretty things, as most girls do.

31
00:02:43.964 --> 00:02:47.787
But what can one do if family finances don't permit such treats?

32
00:02:49.829 --> 00:02:50.770
Next comes me.

33
00:02:51.911 --> 00:02:55.414
As I mentioned, the author Louisa and I share many traits.

34
00:02:56.414 --> 00:02:59.157
I am also a writer and I love to read.

35
00:02:59.897 --> 00:03:05.682
I'm not pretty like Meg or gentle like Beth, but I have a very strong personality, as my

36
00:03:05.782 --> 00:03:06.783
family will tell you.

37
00:03:08.304 --> 00:03:12.788
My biggest weak point is my short temper and I often lose control of it.

38
00:03:13.800 --> 00:03:17.624
It gets me into many arguments and sometimes causes mishaps.

39
00:03:18.585 --> 00:03:21.007
But I'm loyal and true to my family and friends.

40
00:03:21.908 --> 00:03:23.309
I will do anything for them.

41
00:03:24.330 --> 00:03:27.433
I'm a bit of a tomboy, which means I act like a boy.

42
00:03:28.294 --> 00:03:31.677
In fact, I'll admit I sometimes wish I were a boy.

43
00:03:32.477 --> 00:03:35.220
This kind of thinking also gets me into trouble.

44
00:03:37.282 --> 00:03:39.224
Beth is my darling little sister.

45
00:03:40.048 --> 00:03:44.329
I have a soft spot for her as she is the most gentle and shy creature you will

46
00:03:44.429 --> 00:03:45.309
ever come across.

47
00:03:46.230 --> 00:03:51.811
Like Mother, Beth is very caring and she holds nothing back when it comes to helping others.

48
00:03:52.971 --> 00:03:58.693
Beth never complains or upsets people and she would rather do something herself than be a bother to

49
00:03:58.793 --> 00:04:01.334
others. She loves music.

50
00:04:01.934 --> 00:04:04.555
Her voice is as angelic as her personality.

51
00:04:06.755 --> 00:04:09.656
Finally, there's Amy, the youngest of our clan.

52
00:04:10.844 --> 00:04:14.506
I suppose Amy and I are the pair of sisters who argue the most.

53
00:04:15.567 --> 00:04:18.748
Just between you and me, she irritates me so.

54
00:04:19.669 --> 00:04:22.671
However, I admit Amy does have her good traits.

55
00:04:24.131 --> 00:04:25.372
One of them is her beauty.

56
00:04:26.193 --> 00:04:27.973
She is like a porcelain doll.

57
00:04:28.834 --> 00:04:31.936
When she smiles at you, you forget all your troubles.

58
00:04:32.876 --> 00:04:34.977
She is also a very talented artist.

59
00:04:36.118 --> 00:04:39.540
I wouldn't be surprised if she became a famous painter one day.

60
00:04:40.992 --> 00:04:43.393
One of Amy's weaknesses is her selfishness.

61
00:04:44.393 --> 00:04:47.334
She's the youngest so I can understand this somewhat.

62
00:04:48.234 --> 00:04:53.135
But this characteristic gets her into several scrapes, which Amy thankfully learns from.

63
00:04:55.836 --> 00:05:00.697
So now you know a little about my family and something about Louisa May Alcott.

64
00:05:01.498 --> 00:05:05.659
As I mentioned before, our family lived during the American Civil War.

65
00:05:06.699 --> 00:05:10.340
Life at that time was quite different from what it is like for you today.

66
00:05:10.976 --> 00:05:13.037
For example, look at my clothes.

67
00:05:14.718 --> 00:05:20.141
Not only did we have to wear these long dresses, but when a woman went out, she was

68
00:05:20.221 --> 00:05:22.763
expected to wear gloves and carry a parasol.

69
00:05:23.623 --> 00:05:28.466
Given that I'm a tomboy, can you imagine how difficult it was for me to wear such things?

70
00:05:29.626 --> 00:05:34.169
My sisters had to remind me every time I wasn't dressed in a "ladylike" way.

71
00:05:35.489 --> 00:05:39.832
At this time, women were expected to behave in a certain manner as well.

72
00:05:41.000 --> 00:05:46.084
For most women, their purpose in life consisted of finding a marriage mate and having children.

73
00:05:46.964 --> 00:05:50.847
I resisted such notions and got myself into a lot of trouble for it.

74
00:05:51.847 --> 00:05:56.410
But I, like Louisa, am a firm believer that women should have their independence.

75
00:05:58.132 --> 00:06:01.494
Another thing you might find unusual is our way of life.

76
00:06:02.394 --> 00:06:05.456
It was common in our time to have servants and housekeepers.

77
00:06:06.337 --> 00:06:10.360
My family, as well as Louisa Alcott, hated the idea of slavery.

78
00:06:11.188 --> 00:06:14.149
We would never regard our beloved Hannah as a slave.

79
00:06:14.730 --> 00:06:18.411
She is trusted and loved and is a great help to our family.

80
00:06:20.612 --> 00:06:25.034
Something else you may find peculiar is how the young men and women interact.

81
00:06:26.154 --> 00:06:29.456
In my day, society was much more conservative.

82
00:06:30.316 --> 00:06:35.838
It was not considered proper for young people to date or go out unless they intended to marry.

83
00:06:36.919 --> 00:06:41.917
It's true that many married at a young age, but we had strict rules that allowed or did

84
00:06:41.977 --> 00:06:43.578
not allow certain behaviors.

85
00:06:46.020 --> 00:06:49.381
Time is constantly changing and that can't be helped.

86
00:06:50.262 --> 00:06:53.604
Fashions, manners, customs, and traditions change, too.

87
00:06:54.584 --> 00:07:01.748
Some things, however, are timeless: learning how to grow up, learning how to deal with family issues, learning

88
00:07:01.788 --> 00:07:08.352
to love and respect others, and of course─most important of all─learning who you are.

89
00:07:10.504 --> 00:07:13.326
Little Women is a story about just those things.

90
00:07:14.627 --> 00:07:19.310
Even though it was written more than a hundred years ago, I hope that you will find lessons

91
00:07:19.350 --> 00:07:21.912
you can learn from and apply in your life today.
